    {
      "id": "AqXCHaUPzCx91MSEGBp53",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80.5,
      "y": -1585.30859375,
      "width": 754.9794311523438,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cOj2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1310882616,
      "version": 477,
      "versionNonce": 37401766,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786554714131,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is DNS (Domain Name System) and why do we need it?\n- Humans cannot remember IP addresses but they can remember domain names\n- Computers communicate using IP addresses, not domain names\n- DNS provides a name -> IP address mapping mechanism\n- IP can change while domain remains the same\n- Allows directing users to the nearest server/CDN\n- Can be used for load balancing (not fine grained one)\n- Built on top of UDP, runs on port 53",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is DNS (Domain Name System) and why do we need it?\n- Humans cannot remember IP addresses but they can remember domain names\n- Computers communicate using IP addresses, not domain names\n- DNS provides a name -> IP address mapping mechanism\n- IP can change while domain remains the same\n- Allows directing users to the nearest server/CDN\n- Can be used for load balancing (not fine grained one)\n- Built on top of UDP, runs on port 53",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
